{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbvtXGm4wadsEq47CqFC", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I saved this as a project decision in EngramDB, so other sessions and collaborators will see it whenever they work on the API. The rule: all new or changed public API routes go under `/v2`, and `/v1` is frozen. That means no new routes, fields or behavior changes in `/v1`; changes to a `/v1` endpoint go into its `/v2` version instead.\n\nI searched the repo for anything that might already break this. The only `/v1` matches are two addresses for outside services, not your own routes:\n- the payments sandbox URL in `tests/test_payments.py:4`\n- `LEDGER_URL` in `src/billing/invoices.py:8`\n\nThose are other services' API versions, so the memory notes that the decision doesn't apply to them."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 666, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25359, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 666}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "683bc08b-090b-446e-975b-27da41761fe5", "uuid": "ccec601f-8812-4ca0-9236-e3a189be0bab", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T17:42:21.123Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbvtWvRfwb76bBXRZSbC"}
